# Stripe payment rules

- This project charges listing fees and upgrades. It does not process buyer-to-seller transactions and does not use Stripe Connect in MVP.
- Calculate price and eligibility server-side from versioned internal price definitions. Never trust amounts, product IDs, listing IDs, or entitlements supplied by the browser.
- Create a local Order before creating Stripe Checkout and attach only opaque correlation metadata.
- Browser success/cancel redirects are presentation only. They never establish payment state or activate a listing.
- Only verified Stripe webhooks may establish durable payment truth.
- Verify signatures against the raw request body and the correct environment secret.
- Persist every event ID uniquely before processing. Handlers must be idempotent, replayable, and safe for duplicate/out-of-order delivery.
- Lock or conditionally update rows when applying money/state changes.
- Validate currency, expected amount, order state, account/mode, and referenced objects before granting an entitlement.
- A paid listing transitions to moderation through the listing transition service after the required entitlement is durable.
- Never log full webhook payloads, payment method details, customer personal data, secrets, or success URLs containing session IDs.
- Test live/test isolation, duplicate events, event replay, mismatch handling, delayed events, failed checkout, refunds, and reconciliation.
